# Philosophy audit — round 2

Verdict for philosophical application: NOT SATISFIED. The diary’s new activity makes an inference contradicted by the player’s recorded result (P1). No material misquotation or work/translator misattribution was found in the 45-entry source catalog.

Reviewed 2026-11-01 at commit 32eee0c. Scope: all 45 catalog quotations, their glosses/limits, all 22 session claims and all 111 authored rounds/levels. All catalog quotations were also read from the served `/sources` page on 390×844 touch/mobile and 1440×900 desktop: 45/45 source matches on each. This ledger is source/content analysis; the root review owns full gameplay/design coverage.

## Previous findings

| Earlier ID | Status | Current evidence |
|---|---|---|
| R2 | fixed | `scene-3` now distinguishes truth conditions from the partner’s unique-location requirement. `../early-games/phone/134-after-next.png`; `src/games/scene/rounds.ts:168`. |
| R3 | fixed | `h1-4` wrong feedback now depends on meaning/checking practice; `h1-4b` allows ordinary existence doubt. `../late-games/phone/060-question-answer.png`, `063-next.png`. |
| R11 | fixed | `bb1-1` explicitly disallows every comparison procedure. `../late-games/phone/026-next.png`. |
| R12 | fixed | Served source links now say German original; English translator/publisher/edition and section guidance provided, satisfying the bibliographic alternative in R1. `phone-pi-bibliography.png`, `phone-oc-20.png`, `live-sources.json`. |
| R13 | fixed | Served PI270 uses `shews`; manually compared against printed 95e (`pi-page-51.png`). `phone-pi-270.png`. |
| R14 | fixed | Source gloss distinguishes demonstrative use from subsequent teaching of arch; the successful b3-5 state explicitly performs the naming step. `../early-games/phone/039-builder-ostension.png`, `desktop-pi-6.png`. |

R1’s grammar curriculum has been replaced by four rule-following levels; numerical continuation and signpost examples are philosophical tasks. Residual English copy elsewhere is P2, not a repetition of R1. R4 has changed: activities now exist, but the new diary application fails P1. The root review determines R4’s overall gameplay status.

## Remaining findings

**P1 — major — The diary claims a predictive use even when every prediction fails.**

Where: `http://localhost:3417/play/beetle`, Sessions → The diary, `bb2-0`; `src/games/choice/activities.tsx:267` and `:275`; content `src/games/beetle/rounds.ts:133` and `:145`. Served evidence: `../late-games/phone-edges/diary-zero-matches-completed.png`, `../late-games/desktop-edges/diary-zero-matches.png`, and `../late-games/edges.json`.

Mark days 2–6 Not S / S / Not S / S / Not S, reveal the gauge, and complete. The screen reports 0 of 5 matches while concluding that S reports rising blood pressure without the gauge. It awards full completion. PI270 begins from a discovered reliable correlation; it does not say attaching an arbitrary failed diary to a public instrument makes it predictive. Merely providing a criterion does not establish successful use by that criterion. The source quotation is correct; this application is not.

Concrete fix: let the player discover/correct and test a correlation. When marks fail, say the diary does not yet predict the gauge, and require or demonstrate a calibrated use before that conclusion. Preserve the distinction between correctness against a public criterion and success in applying it. A successful prediction establishes practical use, not verification of a private sensation’s identity; PI270 explicitly makes private recognition indifferent once the use works. The initial phase also supplies publicly comparable visible shapes and a persistent day-1 sample, so its claim that only an impression exists needs an explicit toy-model limitation or a better activity design.

Primary comparison: [Anscombe, PI270, printed 94e–95e / PDF page 51](https://static1.squarespace.com/static/54889e73e4b0a2c1f9891289/t/564b61a4e4b04eca59c4d232/1447780772744/Ludwig.Wittgenstein.-.Philosophical.Investigations.pdf#page=51). The downloaded scan was visually inspected in `pi-page-51.png`; the earlier review’s page-52 pointer was off by one for this file.

**P2 — minor — An English plural lesson survives in a builder hint.**

Where: `http://localhost:3417/play/builder`, `builder-2`, `b2-1`; `src/games/builder/rounds.ts:84`. The hint teaches adding -s to most nouns. It is not needed to perform or understand the philosophical distinction between quantity words, object words and pointing, and the brief explicitly excludes English as a learning goal.

Concrete fix: replace it with …185 tokens truncated…hanged from the second edition. Part I section references and Part II xi passage checked.
- [On Certainty, Paul & Anscombe, Blackwell 1969 scan](https://www.circuitdebater.org/circuitdebater/archive/w/file/view/On%20Certainty.pdf/507953768/On%20Certainty.pdf): retrieved successfully this turn. The earlier prawfsblawg URL returned 403, so it was not relied upon as an accessible reader link.

`node qa/codex-review-r2/philosophy/extract.cjs` exports the actual authored data. `uv run --with pymupdf --with beautifulsoup4 python qa/codex-review-r2/philosophy/fetch_primary.py` retrieved all three primary editions. `python qa/codex-review-r2/philosophy/compare_quotes.py` found normalized exact excerpt matches for 39/45 quotations; remaining pi-8/pi-19/pi-270/oc-97/oc-125/oc-341 were manually checked against rendered pages. Their failures were OCR (including numeric 1 versus i), line/column extraction or inserted page headings, not catalog wording defects. Ellipses and typographic quotation-mark changes were respected, not mistaken for omissions. `python qa/codex-review-r2/philosophy/live_sources.py` confirmed all 45 served quotations on both devices with zero source-text mismatches. All eight live screenshots and eight rendered scan pages created by these checks were viewed. No application files or server process were changed.

The ledger below marks a quotation match separately from whether the authored teaching application is supported. “Supported” does not imply that a small game establishes the entire philosophical argument or that every scholar accepts the same interpretation. The café scenes are local authored examples, not universal interpersonal rules. The ladder/limits are explanatory material; a quotation’s accuracy alone does not prove these ideas are learned by playing.

