# Jackson 知识库索引

> AI Agent：回答问题前先读此文件，找到相关页面后再深入阅读。
> 人类：按 Ctrl+F 搜索关键词，或在 Obsidian 中 Ctrl+O 直接跳转。

## 使用说明

- 每个条目格式：`[[文件名]] — 一行摘要`
- 按领域分组，新文件加到对应分组下
- AI 在创建新 .md 文件后应更新此索引
- 旧知识库归档在 `D:\Jackson-archive\`，可从中提取文件补充回来

---

## 知识库架构
"""Measure a website's default requirements: mobile-first layout, touch, speed, SEO and the
measurable part of the user's design taste: readable contrast, no gradient text, no emoji icons
and one language per page (FAIL: the user's explicit bans), and on landing pages a product visual, no repeated "heading + cards"
grids and no empty-slogan H1 (WARN). The user's site constraints (2026-10-28) add the core task in the
first phone screen, GEO (served HTML, AI crawlers, llms.txt), accessibility that also lets agents use
the page, and one analytics tool.

User decision (2026-10-21): a website is responsive by default. Mobile experience,
interaction, interface, speed and SEO are required even when the request never mentions
them (website-experience.md §0). This script measures what a browser can measure; it does
not replace the walkthrough (§2.7).

    python scripts/web-check.py <url> [<url> ...] [--out DIR] [--app] [--allow-noindex]
                                [--storage-state FILE]

Pass every page the change touched. Run it against a production build or the deployed URL: a
dev server ships unminified JavaScript and fails the speed budget for reasons the real site does
not have. `--app` is for pages behind sign-in (dashboards, settings): search checks are skipped,
layout, touch and speed still apply. `--storage-state` loads a Playwright session for them.

Mobile: 375x812 CSS px, touch, DPR 3, 4G-class network (150 ms RTT, 1.6 Mbps down) and 4x
CPU slowdown, the same order as Lighthouse's mobile preset. Desktop: 1440x900, no throttling.
Writes <out>/web-check.json plus mobile-<n>.png and desktop-<n>.png per page. Each check is
PASS, WARN or FAIL; the overall verdict is FAIL when any check fails. Exit 0 PASS, 1 FAIL, 2
tool error. Speed FAILs only on the Core Web Vitals poor lines, and LCP is judged after the
first byte, because this host's distance to a foreign server is not the page's cost (the time
to first byte is reported and warned on separately). Lab numbers are approximate; field data
(CrUX, PageSpeed Insights) is the final word for a live site.
"""
import argparse
import base64
import html
import ipaddress
import json
import re
import sys
import time
from datetime import datetime, timezone
from pathlib import Path
from urllib.parse import urljoin, urlparse

VERSION = 2
MOBILE = {"width": 375, "height": 812}
DESKTOP = {"width": 1440, "height": 900}
MOBILE_UA = ("Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 14; Pixel 8) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) "
             "Chrome/141.0 Mobile Safari/537.36")
NETWORK = {"offline": False, "latency": 150, "downloadThroughput": 1_600_000 / 8,
           "uploadThroughput": 750_000 / 8}
CPU_SLOWDOWN = 4
# (warn above, fail above; None never fails). LCP is measured from the first byte: the Core Web
# Vitals 2.5 s / 4 s lines less a typical 0.5 s first byte. TBT and bytes are lab proxies that
# vary with this host's CPU, so they warn. A review found github.com, stripe.com and vercel.com
# failing on TBT and raw LCP from this network.
BUDGETS = {"lcp_render_ms": (2000, 3500), "cls": (0.1, 0.25), "ttfb_ms": (800, None), "tbt_ms": (200, None),
           "transfer_kb": (1600, None), "js_kb": (350, None)}

# Collected from the first byte, before the page's own scripts run.
OBSERVERS = """
window.__wc = {lcp: null, cls: 0, tbt: 0, ttfb: null};
const watch = (type, fn) => { try { new PerformanceObserver(l => l.getEntries().forEach(fn)).observe({type, buffered: true}); } catch (e) {} };
watch('largest-contentful-paint', e => { window.__wc.lcp = e.renderTime || e.loadTime || e.startTime; });
watch('layout-shift', e => { if (!e.hadRecentInput) window.__wc.cls += e.value; });
watch('longtask', e => { window.__wc.tbt += Math.max(0, e.duration - 50); });
watch('navigation', e => { window.__wc.ttfb = e.responseStart; });
"""

DOM_PROBE = r"""
() => {
  const de = document.documentElement, body = document.body || de;
  const cw = de.clientWidth, sw = Math.max(de.scrollWidth, body.scrollWidth);
  const shown = el => { const r = el.getBoundingClientRect(), s = getComputedStyle(el);
    return r.width > 4 && r.height > 4 && s.visibility !== 'hidden' && s.display !== 'none' && parseFloat(s.opacity) > 0; };
  const name = el => { const cls = typeof el.className === 'string' ? el.className.trim().split(/\s+/).slice(0, 2).join('.') : '';
    const text = (el.innerText || el.value || el.getAttribute('aria-label') || el.getAttribute('alt') || '').trim().replace(/\s+/g, ' ');
    return (el.tagName.toLowerCase() + (el.id ? '#' + el.id : '') + (cls ? '.' + cls : '')).slice(0, 60) + (text ? ' "' + text.slice(0, 30) + '"' : ''); };
  const scrollsX = el => { for (let p = el.parentElement; p && p !== body; p = p.parentElement) {
    const o = getComputedStyle(p).overflowX; if (o === 'auto' || o === 'scroll') return true; } return false; };
  const all = Array.from(body.querySelectorAll('*'));
  const wide = [], clipped = [];
  for (const el of all) {
    if (wide.length >= 5 && clipped.length >= 5) break;
    const r = el.getBoundingClientRect();
    if (r.right <= cw + 1 || !shown(el) || scrollsX(el)) continue;
    if (sw > cw + 1) { if (wide.length < 5) wide.push(name(el)); }
    else if (r.left < cw - 1 && (el.innerText || '').trim() && clipped.length < 5) clipped.push(name(el));
  }
  // Touch targets: WCAG 2.5.8 (24 px, or a 24 px circle that touches no other target) and the 44 px design goal.
  const sel = 'a[href],button,input:not([type=hidden]),select,textarea,summary,[role=button],[role=link],[onclick]';
  const targets = [];
  for (let el of body.querySelectorAll(sel)) {
    if (/^(checkbox|radio)$/.test(el.type || '') && el.closest('label')) el = el.closest('label');
    if (!shown(el)) continue;
    const r = el.getBoundingClientRect();
    if (r.right < 0 || r.left > cw) continue;
    // A link inside a sentence is exempt (WCAG 2.5.8 inline); a row of links is not a sentence.
    const parent = el.parentElement, links = parent ? Array.from(parent.querySelectorAll(sel)) : [];
    const prose = ((parent && parent.innerText) || '').replace(/\s+/g, '').length
      - links.reduce((n, a) => n + (a.innerText || '').replace(/\s+/g, '').length, 0);
    if (el.tagName === 'A' && getComputedStyle(el).display === 'inline' && prose >= 10) continue;
    targets.push({el, r, cx: r.left + r.width / 2, cy: r.top + r.height / 2, small: Math.min(r.width, r.height) < 24});

