- Actual touch taps were used in the phone café correction check and the sign-language path; the main journey used Playwright clicks in a mobile/touch browser context.
- Initial scene edge attempts used an unavailable placement target, then a disabled submit button. These were review-script mistakes, not product failures. The completed edge script uses a valid key placement and verifies its restoration; the main full journey independently tests a wrong scene and correction.

Learning judgments: builder requires actions within a shared practice and distinguishes orders/reports; scene manipulates truth conditions and negation; café makes the same words require different responses in different contexts; family constructs chains with overlapping features. No residual English-course framing was found in these four games after the builder hint change. Retention was not measured. The Tractatus limit/ladder content remains mostly explanatory; it is not a new regression or independently enacted lesson.

Not covered: physical hardware; Safari/Firefox; screen-reader speech; every input permutation; full keyboard-only journeys; independent learning/retention assessment; automated accessibility scans of every gameplay state (parent handles route scans); full-page phone capture of every end card; scholarly judgment beyond the specific live behavior described here.
